Done. Both changes build, existing tests pass, and the CLI filtering works end-to-end.

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match via `==` (not substring), preserves relative order (iterates in source order, no reordering).

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — `list` now scans trailing `--tag <TAG>` args and, when present, routes through `filter_by_tag(&notes, tag)`; otherwise prints all notes as before. Imported `filter_by_tag` from `notekeep`.

Verified: `cargo build` clean, `cargo test` (2/2 pass), and live CLI — `--tag rust` returned only the two rust notes in original order; `--tag swift` returned just the swift note; an unknown tag returned nothing.

One design note: `--tag` is parsed only within the `list` branch, and the flag value is taken as the token immediately following it (no `=` form, no `--tag=rust`).


